{# ============================================================================
   WATCHES — this area's own shift names, the five rules that decide late,
   offline and a valid check-in, and which station runs what.

   PORTED FROM designs/…/modules/roster/configure-watches.html, which is
   variants-watches option A arranged per variants-watches-layout option A
   and the rules card per variants-rules-card option A.

   THE RULINGS THIS PAGE IS, in the owner's words: "users should be able to
   define their shift names", "rules configurable like exceptions", "forcing
   predefined options is stupid". So the product knows NO shift name and NO
   blessed value: a shift is a field this area typed, a rule is a number and
   a unit, and any rule may be given to one station — on that station's own
   row, never in a fourth card listing stations the table above already has.

   COVERAGE MANIFEST — every element of the drawn page.

   | element                          | type    | source                          | interaction        | status |
   |----------------------------------|---------|---------------------------------|--------------------|--------|
   | page subline (the design's)      | chrome  | static + station count          | none               | done   |
   | h2.zone "Watches"                | chrome  | static                          | none               | done   |
   | section intro under the heading  | —       | —                               | —                  | DROPPED 21 sep: the design has none, and it said the subline twice |
   | Shifts card head + caption       | chrome  | static                          | none               | done   |
   | .wsh per shift, data-cat         | data    | Shift.colour                    | —                  | done   |
   | .wpick palette picker (18 slots) | control | Shift.colour + who wears what   | picks a free slot  | done   |
   | input.wnm shift name             | control | Shift.label                     | saved with the grid| done   |
   | .hrs two windows                 | control | Shift.startsAt/endsAt           | saved with the grid| done   |
   | .n "N stations run it"           | data    | watches expecting that key      | none               | done   |
   | a.x close this shift             | control | —                               | closes, never drops| done   |
   | .staddrow + Add a shift          | control | —                               | adds a shift row   | done   |
   | .wfollow follow line             | chrome  | static                          | none               | done   |
   | Rules card head + caption        | chrome  | static                          | none               | done   |
   | .rl × 5 (k / v / m)              | control | ShiftRule, else the standard    | saved with the grid| done   |
   | .rl.chk "say it sooner"          | —       | —                               | —                  | CUT, ruled 21 sep |
   | Discard / Save the rules         | control | —                               | reload / one write | done   |
   | Stations card head + caption     | data    | station and run counts          | none               | done   |
   | table.wmx head, one th per shift | data    | the area's open list            | none               | done   |
   | td.l station name, code · kind   | data    | Station                         | none               | done   |
   | td.n Rangers                     | data    | StationWatch.needsPerShift      | none               | done   |
   | button.wtg per station × shift   | control | StationWatch.expects            | toggles            | done   |
   | .wexcin exceptions + add         | control | StationRuleException            | adds / removes     | done   |
   | tr.none for a station off books  | state   | no watch                        | none               | done   |
   | Discard / Save                   | control | —                               | reload / one write | done   |
   | empty shift list                 | state   | a fresh area names its own      | none               | done   |

   TWO STATED DEPARTURES FROM THE DRAWING, both because a drawing cannot be
   pressed:

   1. THE SHIFTS CARD IS DRAWN WITH NO SAVE. It is a card of editable fields,
      so it needs one; rather than invent a control the design does not have,
      the two cards of the grid are ONE form and the drawn "Save the rules"
      saves both. Adding and closing a shift submit the same form, so neither
      is a way to lose a name somebody had just corrected.
   2. THE DRAWN "1 station run it" IS A TYPO and is written "1 station runs
      it" here.
   ========================================================================== #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiRoster/configure/_frame.html.twig' %}

{# WHETHER THIS PERSON MAY CHANGE HOW THE AREA RUNS ITS ROSTER — the pair
   every write on this page carries. The page itself opens on the ground,
   so a reader sees the setup with every control disabled. #}
{% set mayManage = door('roster.configure', area) %}

{% set save_grid = path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::SAVE_SHIFTS_AND_RULES_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) %}
{% set runs_at_least_one = rows|filter(r => r.runs|filter(v => v)|length > 0)|length %}

{# THE DESIGN'S OWN SUBLINE, as a fragment. It used to be said twice — once
   here and once again as a section intro under the heading — which is what
   made this page read as prose. The intro is gone; the design has none. #}
{% block shell_page_subtitle %}Shifts this area names itself, the rules that decide late, offline and a valid check-in, and which of the {{ rows|length }} station{{ rows|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} runs what{% endblock %}

{% block roster_section %}
{# ONE CONTROLLER FOR THE WHOLE SECTION, and not one per form: the colour
   swatch is in the first form and the station table is in the second, and a
   controller mounted on each would be two instances that have to agree about
   nothing. It is named for its largest job. #}
<div data-controller="roster--station-table">
<h2 class="zone" id="watches">Watches</h2>

<form method="post" action="{{ save_grid }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
    <div class="grid g2">

        {# ---- THIS AREA'S OWN SHIFTS ------------------------------------
           THE PRODUCT KNOWS NONE. A fresh area opens on an empty list and
           names its own; the four in the drawing are what one park typed.
           A shift's COLOUR is a stored palette slot given at creation and
           kept on every surface — never its position in this list, which is
           what used to recolour a park the day somebody reordered it. #}
        <div class="c rband">
            <div class="rb-hd">
                <span class="tab">Shifts</span>
                <span class="rb-ttl">this area&rsquo;s own names, hours and colours &mdash; every sheet, every day board and every station list reads this list</span>
            </div>
            <div class="rb-body">
                {% for shift in shifts %}
                    {% set id = shift.uuid.toRfc4122 %}
                    <div class="wsh" data-cat="{{ shift.colour }}" data-roster-shift>
                        {# THE SLOT THIS SHIFT IS WEARING, POSTED FIRST. A slot
                           picked below carries the same name and, being later
                           in the document, is the value that arrives — so the
                           row posts what it shows whether or not anybody opened
                           the palette. #}
                        <input type="hidden" name="shift_colour_{{ id }}" value="{{ shift.colour }}" data-roster-colour>

                        {# THE PALETTE, NEVER A FREE COLOUR. RULED 21 sep: the
                           house owns eighteen slots and a shift wears one of
                           them, so this is a picker over the eighteen and not a
                           colour input. A slot another shift is wearing is
                           shown with that shift's name and cannot be taken —
                           two shifts in one hue is a fortnight nobody can read.

                           IT IS THE HOUSE DROPDOWN, which is a `<details>`: it
                           opens, chooses and closes with no script of ours, and
                           choosing is a submit, so the picked slot is saved by
                           the same write that saves the names and the hours. #}
                        <details class="i-dd wpick">
                            <summary class="wsw i-ddt" aria-label="The colour of {{ shift.label }}"></summary>
                            <div class="i-ddmenu wpal" aria-label="The shift&rsquo;s colour">
                                <span class="i-ddhead">the palette &middot; {{ freeSlots }} of {{ slots|length }} free</span>
                                <div class="wpalg">
                                    {% for slot, wornBy in slots %}
                                        {% set mine = slot == shift.colour %}
                                        <button type="{{ mine or (wornBy is not null) or not mayManage ? 'button' : 'submit' }}"
                                                class="wsl{{ mine ? ' on' : (wornBy ? ' gone' : '') }}" data-cat="{{ slot }}"
                                                {{ mine or (wornBy is not null) or not mayManage ? 'disabled' : '' }}
                                                name="shift_colour_{{ id }}" value="{{ slot }}"
                                                title="slot {{ slot }} &middot; {{ mine ? 'this shift' : (wornBy ?? 'free') }}"><i></i></button>
                                    {% endfor %}
                                </div>
                                {% if takenBy is not empty %}
                                    <span class="wptaken">taken: {{ takenBy|join(' · ') }}</span>
                                {% endif %}
                                <span class="wpfoot">one palette, never a free colour</span>
                            </div>
                        </details>
                        <input class="fld wnm" name="shift_label_{{ id }}" value="{{ shift.label }}" aria-label="Shift name" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                        <span class="hrs">
                            <input class="wval" name="shift_start_{{ id }}" value="{{ shift.startsAt }}" aria-label="{{ shift.label }} starts at" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                            to
                            <input class="wval" name="shift_end_{{ id }}" value="{{ shift.endsAt }}" aria-label="{{ shift.label }} ends at" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                        </span>
                        <span class="n">{{ runCounts[shift.key]|default(0) }} station{{ runCounts[shift.key]|default(0) == 1 ? ' runs' : 's run' }} it</span>
                        <span class="sp"></span>
                        {% if mayManage %}
                            {# A REAL CONTROL AND NOT A LINK. Closing is a write
                               that needs the page's token, and Stimulus binds
                               no default event to an <a> that goes nowhere. #}
                            <button type="submit" class="x" name="close" value="{{ id }}" title="Close this shift"
                                    formaction="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::CLOSE_SHIFT_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">&times;</button>
                        {% endif %}
                    </div>
                {% else %}
                    <div class="rfrag"><b>This area has named no shift yet</b><em>the product ships none on purpose &mdash; a shift is a word this area chooses, and nothing can be rostered until there is one</em></div>
                {% endfor %}

                <div class="staddrow">
                    {% if mayManage %}
                        <button type="submit" class="btn sm"
                                formaction="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::ADD_SHIFT_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">+ Add a shift</button>
                    {% endif %}
                    <span class="sp"></span>
                    <span class="wfollow">your own names &middot; colour kept on every tab &middot; a shift in use can be closed, not removed</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        {# ---- THE FIVE RULES --------------------------------------------
           A NUMBER AND A UNIT, never a menu of blessed answers. RAISE
           UNFILLED says when a gap is raised as needing a decision, and
           nothing more: a gap is on the sheet the moment it exists, always,
           with no setting — which is why the checkbox the first drawing put
           beside it was cut on 21 sep and is not here. #}
        <div class="c rband">
            <div class="rb-hd">
                <span class="tab">The rules</span>
                <span class="rb-ttl">one row per rule &middot; the last four are what a fill obeys</span>
            </div>
            <div class="rb-body">
                {# ONE HEADING, OVER THE FOUR THAT CAME ACROSS FROM THE SHEET.
                   The rules above it stay an ungrouped list: grouping the
                   whole card under Presence / Check-in / Cover was drawn as
                   variants-rules-card option C and rejected on 21 sep.

                   A RULE IS MEASURED OR IT IS CHOSEN. Two of the filling
                   four have no number in them at all, so the row draws the
                   select the design draws rather than asking somebody to
                   encode "never" as a quantity. #}
                {% for kind in ruleKinds %}
                    {% if kind.isFilling and not (loop.first or ruleKinds[loop.index0 - 1].isFilling) %}
                        <span class="rgrphd">Filling</span>
                    {% endif %}
                    <div class="rl">
                        <span class="k">{{ kind.label }}</span>
                        <span class="v">
                            {% if kind.isChoice %}
                                <select class="fld" name="rule_choice_{{ kind.value }}" aria-label="{{ kind.label }}" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                                    {% for choice in kind.choices %}
                                        <option value="{{ choice.value }}" {{ choice == ruleChoices[kind.value] ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ choice.label }}</option>
                                    {% endfor %}
                                </select>
                            {% else %}
                                {% set value = rules[kind.value] %}
                                <input class="wval n" name="rule_value_{{ kind.value }}" value="{{ value.number }}" aria-label="{{ kind.label }}, how much" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                                <select class="wval u" name="rule_unit_{{ kind.value }}" aria-label="{{ kind.label }}, in what" {{ mayManage ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                                    {% for unit in kind.units %}
                                        <option value="{{ unit.value }}" {{ unit == value.unit ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ unit.label }}</option>
                                    {% endfor %}
                                </select>
                            {% endif %}
                        </span>
                        <span class="m">{{ kind.fragment }}</span>
                    </div>
                {% endfor %}

                {% if mayManage %}
                    <div class="staddrow">
                        <span class="sp"></span>
                        {# DISCARD IS A RELOAD, which is exactly what it means:
                           nothing has been written, so throwing the edits away
                           is asking the server for the page again. #}
                        <a class="btn sm" href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::WATCHES_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">Discard</a>
                        <button type="submit" class="cta">Save the rules</button>
                    </div>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</form>

{# ---- WHICH STATION RUNS WHAT, AND WHAT IT DOES DIFFERENTLY -------------
   ITS OWN FORM, because toggling twelve stations and typing a threshold are
   two acts a duty officer does at two different moments. An exception lives
   on its station's own row (ruled 21 sep): the stations with nothing to say
   are not made to say it. #}
<form method="post" action="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::SAVE_WATCHES_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
    <div class="c rband">
        <div class="rb-hd">
            <span class="tab">Stations</span>
            <span class="rb-ttl">{{ rows|length }} station{{ rows|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} &middot; {{ runs_at_least_one }} run{{ runs_at_least_one == 1 ? 's' : '' }} at least one shift &middot; the last column is what each one does differently</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rb-body">
            <div class="wmxwrap">
                <table class="wmx">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th class="l">Station</th>
                            <th class="l">Rangers</th>
                            {% for shift in shifts %}
                                <th data-cat="{{ shift.colour }}">{{ shift.label }}<em>{{ shift.startsAt }}&ndash;{{ shift.endsAt }}</em></th>
                            {% endfor %}
                            <th class="l">Its own rules</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        {% for row in rows %}
                            {% set station = row.station %}
                            <tr class="{{ row.onTheBooks and row.runs|filter(v => v)|length > 0 ? '' : 'none' }}">
                                {# THE DRAWN "ST-01 · gate" IS A CODE AND A
                                   STATION KIND. The kind is the AREA's field
                                   and the area module has no such column, so
                                   this prints the code and the locality it
                                   does have — naming the gap rather than
                                   inventing a kind here, where a station's
                                   own vocabulary is not this module's to
                                   define. #}
                                <td class="l"><b>{{ station.name }}</b><em>{{ station.code ?: '—' }}{% if station.locality %} &middot; {{ station.locality|lower }}{% endif %}</em></td>
                                {# NULL AND ZERO ARE DIFFERENT FACTS. A station
                                   nobody has stated a need for is short of
                                   nobody; a zero would read as a place that
                                   needs nobody at all. #}
                                <td class="n">{{ row.needs ?? '—' }}</td>
                                {% for shift in shifts %}
                                    <td>
                                        <button type="button" class="wtg {{ row.runs[shift.key] ? 'on' : '' }}"
                                                aria-pressed="{{ row.runs[shift.key] ? 'true' : 'false' }}"
                                                aria-label="{{ station.name }} runs {{ shift.label }}"
                                                data-action="roster--station-table#toggle"
                                                {{ mayManage and row.onTheBooks ? '' : 'disabled' }}>{{ ux_icon('roster:check') }}</button>
                                        <input type="hidden" name="expects_{{ station.id }}[]" value="{{ shift.key }}"
                                               data-roster-expects {{ row.runs[shift.key] ? '' : 'disabled' }}>
                                    </td>
                                {% endfor %}
                                <td class="l">
                                    <div class="wexcin" data-roster-exceptions data-station="{{ station.id }}">
                                        {% for exception in row.exceptions %}
                                            <span class="ln">
                                                <b>{{ exception.kind.label }}</b>{{ exception.value.label }}
                                                <input type="hidden" name="exception_{{ station.id }}_kind[]" value="{{ exception.kind.value }}">
                                                <input type="hidden" name="exception_{{ station.id }}_value[]" value="{{ exception.value.number }}">
                                                <input type="hidden" name="exception_{{ station.id }}_unit[]" value="{{ exception.value.unit.value }}">
                                                {% if mayManage %}
                                                    <button type="button" class="x" title="Follow the area again"
                                                            data-action="roster--station-table#forget">&times;</button>
                                                {% endif %}
                                            </span>
                                        {% endfor %}
                                        {% if mayManage and row.onTheBooks %}
                                            <button type="button" class="add"
                                                    data-action="roster--station-table#except">{{ row.exceptions is empty ? '+ give it its own rule' : '+ another' }}</button>
                                        {% endif %}
                                    </div>
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                        {% else %}
                            <tr><td class="l" colspan="3"><b>This area registers no station</b><em>there is nothing for a roster to watch until it does</em></td></tr>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            {# THE PICKER IS THIS MODULE'S ADDITION TO THE DRAWING, stated
               rather than slipped in: a station joins these books here, and
               a drawing with one park's twelve rows has nowhere to say which
               one. It wears the reference card's own add-row shape. #}
            {% if mayManage %}
                <div class="staddrow">
                    {% if postsOffTheBooks is not empty %}
                        <label class="fldlab" for="roster-add-post">Add a station</label>
                        <select class="fld" id="roster-add-post" name="station">
                            {% for station in postsOffTheBooks %}
                                <option value="{{ station.uuidString }}">{{ station.name }}{% if station.code %} &middot; {{ station.code }}{% endif %}</option>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </select>
                        <button type="submit" class="btn sm"
                                formaction="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::ADD_TO_ROSTER_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">Put it on the books</button>
                    {% endif %}
                    <span class="sp"></span>
                    <a class="btn sm" href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterConfigureController::WATCHES_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">Discard</a>
                    <button type="submit" class="cta">Save</button>
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>

    {# THE SHAPE A NEW EXCEPTION IS STAMPED FROM. One template in the markup
       rather than a string inside the controller: the kinds and the units it
       offers are the SERVER's list, and a script that built the select from
       its own copy would be a second vocabulary going stale. #}
    <template data-roster-exception-template>
        <span class="ln">
            {# THE MEASURED RULES ONLY. A station may overrule a chosen rule
               too — the service takes one — but this row is a number and a
               unit, and offering a kind it cannot express would be offering
               a control that silently saves nothing. The chosen pair get
               their own row when the design draws one. #}
            <select class="wval u" data-roster-field="kind" aria-label="Which rule">
                {% for kind in ruleKinds|filter(k => not k.isChoice) %}
                    <option value="{{ kind.value }}">{{ kind.label }}</option>
                {% endfor %}
            </select>
            <input class="wval n" value="1" data-roster-field="value" aria-label="How much">
            <select class="wval u" data-roster-field="unit" aria-label="In what">
                {% for kind in ruleKinds|filter(k => not k.isChoice) %}
                    {% for unit in kind.units %}
                        <option value="{{ unit.value }}" data-for="{{ kind.value }}">{{ unit.label }}</option>
                    {% endfor %}
                {% endfor %}
            </select>
            <button type="button" class="x" title="Follow the area again"
                    data-action="roster--station-table#forget">&times;</button>
        </span>
    </template>
</form>
</div>
{% endblock %}
